    /// <summary>
    /// MLEDIT's crosses (CC, OC, MC) of a closed multiline against the records AutoCAD 2021 left (accoreconsole, read back
    /// through <c>DxfOut</c> of a <c>Wblock</c>), STANDARD at scale 20 justified at the top. Where two segments of a closed
    /// multiline can be crossed (a horizontal y = 50 from x = -20 to 220 across the rectangle (0, 0)-(200, 0)-(200, 100)-(0, 100)
    /// meets its right edge and its left), AutoCAD takes the crossing nearest the picks, the distance along each multiline
    /// from its pick added, with a closed multiline's distance along itself from its start the shorter way round: the left
    /// edge's crossing is 550 along the rectangle's 600 and counts as 50. Picked on the bottom edge at (70, 0), the second
    /// at (175, 50) leaves the left edge broken and at (185, 50) the right edge; two crossings as near as each other go to
    /// the earlier segment. Each row is the option, the points of the first multiline ("c:" before them for a closed
    /// one), those of the second, where each is picked and what AutoCAD answered, as <see cref="MlineTeePairTests"/> writes
    /// them; rows where a cross runs the second past its end and AutoCAD draws a stray piece there are left out.
    /// </summary>
    public class MlineClosedCrossPickTests
